WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.126 --> 00:00:15.890
That same morning Tom woke up before it was light.

2
00:00:17.711 --> 00:00:20.232
He thought he was back in his family's room on Offal Street.

3
00:00:20.252 --> 00:00:23.033
"Hey, Nancy, wake up!"

4
00:00:23.433 --> 00:00:24.934
he called softly to his sister.

5
00:00:24.954 --> 00:00:28.215
"I just had a dream that I was king!

6
00:00:29.036 --> 00:00:29.876
Can you believe it?"

7
00:00:32.489 --> 00:00:35.331
A shadowy form appeared next to Tom's bed in the palace.

8
00:00:35.351 --> 00:00:38.612
"Did you call, Your Majesty?"

9
00:00:40.193 --> 00:00:41.274
"Your Majesty?"

10
00:00:42.975 --> 00:00:43.876
Tom groaned.

11
00:00:43.896 --> 00:00:48.298
"Oh, then it wasn't a dream after all."

12
00:00:50.540 --> 00:00:51.720
Tom fell back to sleep.

13
00:00:53.361 --> 00:00:57.504
Soon he was happily dreaming about a pot of gold coins buried next to a tree.

14
00:00:59.304 --> 00:01:02.865
In this dream Tom dug up the coins and hurried home to his mother.

15
00:01:02.885 --> 00:01:05.906
"These are all for you, Mother.

16
00:01:07.086 --> 00:01:08.667
You'll never be hungry again!"

17
00:01:10.607 --> 00:01:12.588
Tom proudly dropped the coins in her lap.

18
00:01:12.608 --> 00:01:16.749
"And I didn't steal or beg for any of them!"

19
00:01:18.209 --> 00:01:22.570
Gathering Tom into her arms, his mother said, "It's late, Your Majesty.

20
00:01:23.611 --> 00:01:24.771
Are you ready to get up?"

21
00:01:27.211 --> 00:01:28.492
"Ugh!" Tom cried.

22
00:01:29.644 --> 00:01:31.566
That was not the answer he was expecting.

23
00:01:33.527 --> 00:01:36.809
He opened his eyes and realized once again that he was still king.

24
00:01:36.829 --> 00:01:41.233
"And I'm still a prisoner in this palace," he thought.

25
00:01:41.253 --> 00:01:45.556
"Time to get dressed, sir," the servant said.

26
00:01:47.557 --> 00:01:50.880
When he sat up, Tom noticed more servants standing around his room.

27
00:01:50.900 --> 00:01:54.942
"Why are there so many people here?"

28
00:01:55.303 --> 00:01:56.684
he asked the first servant.

29
00:01:58.520 --> 00:02:01.482
"To assist Your Majesty with the morning ritual of dressing."

30
00:02:01.502 --> 00:02:04.243
"I can dress myself!"

31
00:02:04.684 --> 00:02:05.484
Tom snapped.

32
00:02:07.746 --> 00:02:13.009
He heard a sharp intake of breath from one servant and realized he'd made a mistake.

33
00:02:13.029 --> 00:02:14.730
"Or you can all help me."

34
00:02:18.252 --> 00:02:19.513
The servants formed a line.

35
00:02:20.933 --> 00:02:24.616
Starting near the door, each garment was passed down the line until it reached Tom.

36
00:02:26.940 --> 00:02:29.941
"This is going to take forever," Tom thought.

37
00:02:31.842 --> 00:02:32.442
And it did.

38
00:02:34.903 --> 00:02:38.725
At last there was only one more garment to go—a silk stocking.

39
00:02:40.566 --> 00:02:42.566
Slowly it made its way toward Tom.

40
00:02:44.727 --> 00:02:48.509
But when the stocking reached the servant closest to Tom, the man held it up.

41
00:02:51.030 --> 00:02:52.470
"Look at that hole!

42
00:02:53.751 --> 00:02:56.372
The king can't wear a less than perfect stocking!"

43
00:02:57.620 --> 00:03:02.502
He handed the stocking to the servant behind him, and it slowly returned to the last servant.

44
00:03:05.142 --> 00:03:09.604
After some delay a perfect stocking was found and sent down the line to Tom.

45
00:03:12.685 --> 00:03:14.525
He put that on along with his shoe.

46
00:03:14.545 --> 00:03:19.027
"I hope this is the end because I'm hungry."

47
00:03:21.247 --> 00:03:23.608
Tom stood up and admired himself in the mirror.

48
00:03:26.148 --> 00:03:35.091
"I'm sorry, Your Majesty, but you can't leave your room until the royal hairdresser has styled your hair."

49
00:03:35.891 --> 00:03:37.971
Tom groaned and sat down again.

50
00:03:37.991 --> 00:03:43.493
"Bring on the combs and brushes, and let's get this over with!"

51
00:03:46.294 --> 00:03:50.475
After breakfast Tom met with his royal advisers around a large table.

52
00:03:51.995 --> 00:03:54.196
Each of them had something for Tom to approve.

53
00:03:56.724 --> 00:04:00.787
Lord Hertford sat at Tom's side, whispering helpful advice as needed.

54
00:04:00.807 --> 00:04:13.477
"Sign and date this document Give your consent for that meeting Refuse to approve that expense Tom remembered

55
00:04:13.537 --> 00:04:15.318
playing with his friends from Offal Street.

56
00:04:15.338 --> 00:04:20.362
"Julian and the others were better royal advisers," he thought.

57
00:04:20.382 --> 00:04:23.204
"They were much more fun!"

58
00:04:25.836 --> 00:04:30.198
The royal treasurer read an accounting of the expenses for King Henry's household.

59
00:04:30.218 --> 00:04:34.281
"What?" Tom gasped.

60
00:04:34.301 --> 00:04:36.862
"That's a lot of money!"

61
00:04:36.882 --> 00:04:40.084
"Yes, Your Majesty."

62
00:04:41.364 --> 00:04:44.206
The treasurer showed Tom the number in her account book.

63
00:04:44.226 --> 00:04:48.688
"And most of that money is still owed."

64
00:04:48.708 --> 00:04:52.591
"You mean we haven't been paying our bills?"

65
00:04:53.851 --> 00:04:54.952
Tom was horrified.

66
00:04:56.220 --> 00:05:01.221
Many people on Offal Street couldn't pay their bills, but he expected the royal family to do so.

67
00:05:03.022 --> 00:05:05.183
The royal treasurer adjusted her glasses.

68
00:05:05.203 --> 00:05:06.903
"That's right, sir.

69
00:05:08.063 --> 00:05:12.525
The royal bank accounts are almost empty, and the servants haven't been paid."

70
00:05:12.545 --> 00:05:17.006
"We will have to economize at once!"

71
00:05:17.466 --> 00:05:18.126
Tom said.

72
00:05:18.146 --> 00:05:23.548
"First of all, we should sell this palace and move somewhere less expensive.

73
00:05:25.924 --> 00:05:27.925
I know of a little house by the fish market.

74
00:05:28.806 --> 00:05:30.247
Perhaps we could move there."

75
00:05:34.229 --> 00:05:38.611
Tom felt a sharp pressure on his arm and knew it was a signal from Lord Hertford.

76
00:05:39.672 --> 00:05:40.572
He stopped talking.

77
00:05:42.653 --> 00:05:46.075
He remembered his dream about giving his mother the pot of gold coins.

78
00:05:47.616 --> 00:05:50.478
Apparently he couldn't do that even as king.

79
00:05:50.498 --> 00:05:57.086
"Maybe I could make my mother a duchess," he thought as a secretary droned on about the late

80
00:05:57.146 --> 00:05:57.846
king's will.

81
00:05:59.788 --> 00:06:01.329
But then he looked around the table.

82
00:06:02.450 --> 00:06:05.191
These advisers were the ones who kept the kingdom running.

83
00:06:06.812 --> 00:06:11.315
If he suggested making his mother the Duchess of Offal Street, they'd think he was ill.

84
00:06:12.476 --> 00:06:13.777
And then they'd do nothing.

85
00:06:16.939 --> 00:06:21.142
The dull work went on until Tom's head began to nod and he fell asleep.

86
00:06:24.448 --> 00:06:25.469
Lord Hertford sighed.

87
00:06:25.489 --> 00:06:30.152
"We have to stop now," he whispered to the others.

88
00:06:30.172 --> 00:06:35.076
"We can't do anything more without the king's signature."
